      },
      "lineNbr": 987,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-05T22:01:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well... it\u0027s valid for a little while, but if we hit this condition the modem has crashed/hung, so I think the safer thing to do is to set it to null so that it doesn\u0027t mislead some other component that didn\u0027t check the (currently ill-defined) timestamp. The question is: would you rather have stale info or a clear signal that something is wrong?",
      "parentUuid": "812f3c9e_a3807053",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 986,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 987,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "b2dcbdf765f2cbc2f9f903ce250582a32d83ec2f",
