      "writtenOn": "2018-09-10T18:27:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "tl;dr Done.\n\nSince we are going to properly expose timeout this release (if I get that far), I suppose it\u0027s reasonable to expect callers not to look at stale results forever and expect them to be meaningful. Besides, we can hope that APM or an SSR brings the modem back online before they get *too* stale. I\u0027d still prefer to clear the result here, but I see both sides. I\u0027ll leave the cached info there and just add an error message so it\u0027s easy to find if we debug this.",
      "parentUuid": "ea57dd1c_08c45adb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 986,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 987,
        "endChar": 79
